== 3. Honest evaluation: threshold chosen on training folds (5-fold, grouped by market), applied to held-out fold
  composite, target 99% on train -> held-out coverage=42.5% accuracy=98.57% (7 errors of 490; Wilson 95% [97.1,99.3])
  composite, target 97% on train -> held-out coverage=54.4% accuracy=96.81% (20 errors of 627; Wilson 95% [95.1,97.9])
  composite, target 95% on train -> held-out coverage=62.8% accuracy=94.75% (38 errors of 724; Wilson 95% [92.9,96.2])

== 4. A learned gate (logistic regression on votes, confidences, answer) evaluated out-of-fold
  out-of-fold AURC: learned gate=0.0594 vs composite=0.0513; coverage@97%: gate=55.0% composite=54.0%; @95%: gate=60.9% composite=62.4%
  Brier of P(majority correct): gate (out-of-fold)=0.1207; mean confidence used as probability=0.1366; constant base rate=0.1428
  AURC difference (gate - composite), cluster bootstrap 95% CI: [+0.0013, +0.0173]

